{"id": "EUVD-2026-101068", "enisaUuid": "86cc4864-3896-367c-a516-43ce7174fb77", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrop_monitor: fix out-of-bounds write in reset_per_cpu_data()\n\nIn reset_per_cpu_data(), al is computed as:\n\n    al = sizeof(struct net_dm_alert_msg);\n    al += dm_hit_limit * sizeof(struct net_dm_drop_point);\n    al += sizeof(struct nlattr);\n\n    skb = genlmsg_new(al, GFP_KERNEL);\n    ...\n    nla = nla_reserve(skb, NLA_UNSPEC, sizeof(struct net_dm_alert_msg));\n    ...\n    msg = nla_data(nla);\n    memset(msg, 0, al);\n\nBecause al includes sizeof(struct nlattr) (the 4-byte attribute header),\ngenlmsg_new() allocates al bytes of tailroom starting at nla.\nHowever, msg points to nla_data(nla), which is located\nsizeof(struct nlattr) bytes past nla. Calling memset(msg, 0, al)\ntherefore writes al bytes starting from msg, exceeding the allocated\nbuffer by sizeof(struct nlattr) (4 bytes) and corrupting\nskb_shared_info.\n\nFix this by letting al represent only the payload length, allocating\nthe skb with genlmsg_new(nla_total_size(al), GFP_KERNEL), and zeroing\nal bytes from msg.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T13:27:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:19:12", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/caf09c09e0f323015ab6777ed1bad5aa10688631", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/56b12f0cd476e4d90a0e2663a80102b388ebf78c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/88d640efd655b10f9fa4e381caf777da1f17c2a6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d54a044136b129822715e8798899af540ec7a9e9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8a04047c6dbff2f49a561b1ff53b043f4807e855", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/530ae0a1458078c7a81fbffd9ff17d42129364d9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/03b672eba4937ff18337049824a114012d57f202", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/439f392084f8f7f59ab9d47a9579185accefe1d8"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6j59-9ph5-7p77", "CVE-2026-98419"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1a976987-d493-315b-a6ec-b67835bfb3f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "214b2cea-e89d-3766-9710-f88a8491f6c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "683703a26e4677db437a1480682851e27c7a154f <88d640efd655b10f9fa4e381caf777da1f17c2a6"}, {"id": "2ce02312-9968-3ad5-a1f8-49872dde59c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "34252ad3-9227-3e78-9d39-91d5ed2ceada", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "409c9d64-f843-3f24-8ef7-6966d63b0597", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "683703a26e4677db437a1480682851e27c7a154f <56b12f0cd476e4d90a0e2663a80102b388ebf78c"}, {"id": "5366e33b-f7c5-3d7f-8fab-df61135fb676", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "610cec89-a891-3686-a47a-ec28c40ebd2a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "683703a26e4677db437a1480682851e27c7a154f <caf09c09e0f323015ab6777ed1bad5aa10688631"}, {"id": "6304e4df-228e-36de-b4c4-069714cba7d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "641bf261-32a8-3512-8fb6-b3b55a99816c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "95552e03-6330-3e7f-b4e2-ad6b7dc4e327", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "9d357b08-7722-30aa-a2d9-9b475b4ec481", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "683703a26e4677db437a1480682851e27c7a154f <d54a044136b129822715e8798899af540ec7a9e9"}, {"id": "ad77d1c3-aff0-300b-bb21-9ab741a64e30", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.31"}, {"id": "a